diff --git a/README_V046.md b/README_V046.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7bd75aa
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README_V046.md
@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@
+# LazyIPDCA-QCQP v0.4.6 — full affine-objective majorant
+
+The v0.4.5 A4X12 run did not enter the outer optimization. Phase I returned a
+feasible point, but the first Lazy-DCA master contained only the three initially
+near-active inequalities while the objective was affine. The omitted
+inequalities were therefore allowed to contain the directions that bound the
+objective. The resulting first Newton direction was enormous: its exact
+quadratic trial residual reached approximately `3.85e15`, the accepted primal
+step was about `4.66e-10`, and the dual step was `0.5`. The second Newton system
+then suffered a complementarity-product explosion and the inner solve stopped
+with `outer_iterations = 0`.
+
+v0.4.6 corrects the model and the primal-dual step together.
+
+## Complete majorant for moderate affine-objective QCQPs
+
+When the original objective Hessian is zero and the number of nonlinear
+inequalities is at most `dca_affine_full_constraint_limit` (default `4096`),
+Lazy-DCA retains every inequality majorant for the whole solve. Working-set
+activation and dropping are disabled in this mode. This is necessary because a
+restricted master with an affine objective need not be bounded even when the
+complete convex majorant is bounded.
+
+The inner solver still receives an already-convex QCQP. It performs no DC
+convexification or curvature discovery. Negative curvature in an original
+constraint is handled once by the outer Lazy-DCA majorant construction.
+
+The mode is reported as
+
+```text
+[LAZY-DCA] ... constraint_set=full-affine-objective ws=<number of inequalities>
+```
+
+It can be controlled with
+
+```text
+--dca-affine-full-limit N
+--no-dca-affine-full
+```
+
+## Coupled nonlinear-residual LazyQP step
+
+The primal and dual parts of one Newton direction now use the common step
+
+```text
+alpha = min(alpha_primal_max, alpha_dual_max).
+```
+
+This prevents a rejected or heavily damped primal displacement from being
+combined with an almost full multiplier displacement. Verbose output reports
+`a`, `apmax`, and `admax`.
+
+The slack remains an independent primal variable. The exact quadratic remainder
+is absorbed into the slack only as far as strict positivity permits; any
+remaining defect is evaluated in the exact nonlinear primal residual and
+corrected at subsequent Newton steps.
+
+## KKT representation and regularization
+
+For `n <= exact_eigen_threshold`, retained rank-one objective and constraint
+corrections are condensed exactly into the primal Hessian block. This avoids a
+large bordered system when a complete majorant contains many corrected rows.
+For a 130-variable, one-equality, 384-inequality model, the resulting KKT
+system has dimension `515`, independently of the number of retained rank-one
+corrections.
+
+The representation is reported as
+
+```text
+[LAZYQP-KKT] n=... eq=... ineq=... lowrank=... representation=condensed dimension=...
+```
+
+Fixed primal and dual KKT shifts are now assembled consistently by `native`,
+`ldl`, `qdldl`, and `mumps`. In adaptive mode, the caller inserts the current
+shifts exactly once. Failed solves, failed globalization, or extremely short
+coupled steps may increase the numerical primal shift and retry the same inner
+iteration.
diff --git a/VALIDATION_v0.4.6.md b/VALIDATION_v0.4.6.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2f42764
--- /dev/null
+++ b/VALIDATION_v0.4.6.md
@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+# Validation — v0.4.6 full affine-objective majorant
+
+## Local release gate
+
+- version: `LazyIPDCA-QCQP 0.4.6-lazyqp-full-majorant (API 460)`;
+- native Release build: PASS without compiler warnings;
+- native Release CTest: **28/28 PASS**;
+- AddressSanitizer + UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer CTest: **28/28 PASS**;
+- existing restoration, SQP, KKT-stop, working-set, backend, curvature-wall,
+  and convex-QCQP regressions: PASS.
+
+## New failure-specific contracts
+
+### Affine master bounded only by an omitted constraint
+
+`lazy_dca_affine_full_majorant` minimizes an affine objective with no finite
+variable bounds and one initially inactive quadratic ball constraint. A lazy
+master that omits the ball is singular/unbounded and never completes the first
+outer subproblem. The full-majorant mode solves it in one outer iteration and
+returns the boundary minimizer.
+
+### A4X12-shaped structural surrogate
+
+`lazy_dca_affine_full_shape_130_1_384` uses:
+
+- 130 variables;
+- one equality;
+- 384 quadratic inequalities;
+- an affine objective;
+- 192 negative-curvature constraint directions.
+
+The exact low-rank corrections are condensed into the primal block. The test
+solves in one outer iteration, enters the optimization, retains all constraints,
+and returns the known feasible minimizer.
+
+This is a structural regression, not the CUTEst A4X12 data set.
+
+### Coupled primal-dual step
+
+`lazyqp_dual_step_coupling` reproduces a large primal Newton component together
+with many barrier rows. It requires the coupled-step path to converge rather
+than applying a large multiplier update after the primal step is backtracked.
+
+### Exact low-rank condensation
+
+`lazyqp_lowrank_condensation` solves the same convex QCQP with the rank-one
+terms represented once by explicit KKT borders and once by exact condensation.
+The two primal solutions agree to the test tolerance.
+
+### Fixed native KKT shifts
+
+`lazyqp_fixed_native_shift` verifies that a flat native KKT system is singular
+when both fixed shifts are zero and is factorizable when the configured primal
+and dual shifts are nonzero.
+
+## External A4X12 gate
+
+The exact exported `A4X12.qcq` is not included in the source-only release, so
+this local validation does not claim final A4X12 convergence. Run
+`tools/run_a4x12_v046_lazyqp.sh` in the `pf_gpu` CUTEst environment.
+
+The first required diagnostics are
+
+```text
+[LAZY-DCA] ... constraint_set=full-affine-objective ws=384
+[LAZYQP-KKT] n=130 eq=1 ineq=384 ... representation=condensed dimension=515
+```
+
+The decisive first gate is `outer_iterations > 0`. Only after that gate passes
+should objective progress and the final original-QCQP KKT certificate be
+assessed.
